    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm working on a 2022 F-150 with a slipping issue. my scan tool is showing some really weird irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit. what are the most likely things causing pressure fluctuations like that in an automatic transmission?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Pressure fluctuations in the hydraulic circuit of a 2022 F-150 can be caused by faulty solenoids, dirty or worn-out nozzle guides, or leaks in the transmission system. Low transmission fluid level, contamination, or incorrect transmission fluid type can also lead to pressure spikes. Additionally, excessive torque or towing capacity can also put additional stress on the transmission system, causing irregular pressure fluctuations. It's recommended to have a professional mechanic inspect your vehicle to diagnose and repair the issue.",
