    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the fluid looks okay on the dipstick but it does seem a bit dark. i'm leaning towards it being a solenoid or maybe something in the valve body. if i pull the pan to check for metal shavings, what kind of debris should i be looking for that would specifically cause these pressure spikes?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
