      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When looking for debris in the transmission pan with a low hydraulic circuit pressure issue, you should be searching for metal shavings or particles that indicate valve body or solenoid component wear. Specifically, look for iridescent white or silver particles that typically come from the solenoids, or small metal spheres that indicate excessive wear on the valve body. These particles can give you a clue about the source of the pressure spikes.",
